-﻿orbitdesign Build 1.65 (based on Community Edition 0.9.184):
+﻿orbitdesign Build 1.66 (based on Community Edition 0.9.184):
 
 * 1.1 FIX: Hardware acceleration stability. Fixed OpenGL extension detection, replaced the deprecated automatic mip map generation that crashed some drivers, checked texture uploads for errors, and added a startup guard that switches hardware acceleration off for one session if ComicRack failed to start last time.
 * 1.2 NEW: Direct2D renderer for the reader. Used by default when hardware acceleration is on, with OpenGL and then software rendering as fallbacks. Handles graphics device resets, uses high quality cubic sampling for "Enable Hardware Filters", and supports paper textures. Start with -hwgl to use the old OpenGL renderer.
@@ -65,6 +65,7 @@
 * 1.63 FIX: The page-count status bar icon that spins while a book's page index is still being read (UpdatePages) is a plain grayscale spinner, nearly invisible against a dark theme's background. Added a white version (Resources\Dark\UpdatePages.gif) and switched it in based on ThemeManager.IsDarkModeEnabled, using the existing ThemeExtensions.InvokeFunc helper - the same light/dark asset-picking convention a few other icons already had files prepared for but nothing was actually wired up to yet.
 * 1.64 NEW: Smarter library quick search. Each word can now match a different field ("aspic poupee" finds Aspic books titled Poupée), accents and full-width characters are ignored ("legendes" finds Légendes), "quoted phrases" match exactly, -word excludes, and field:word restricts a word to one field (writer:, series:, title:, artist:, publisher:, tag:, genre:, character:, year:, number:, file: and more - hover the search box for the list). Smart-list MATCH/NOT queries typed into the box work as before. No slower than the old search.
 * 1.65 FIX: Ctrl+C, Ctrl+X, Ctrl+V and Ctrl+A in the library search boxes now copy, cut, paste and select the search text. The "Copy Data" / "Copy List" menu shortcuts were taking Ctrl+C first, so copying the text put comic data on the clipboard and pasting into Notepad gave nothing.
+* 1.66 NEW: Presets in Book Display Settings (F9). The Preset bar at the bottom-left of the dialog saves everything in it - page effects, curl, paper and reader background, plus the library background, bookshelf and book cover shadow - under a name; picking a preset fills the dialog in, and OK or Apply makes it live. Custom textures are copied into the preset (in a DisplayPresets folder beside the settings), so a preset keeps its pictures even if the original files are moved or deleted.
 
 
